{{/* conditional: shell-owned field-set branches gated by a toggle, shown via
     pure CSS (ADR-005 §7). The plugin declared only the intent; the shell owns
     the toggle and the show/hide — no JavaScript.

     The gate is the same checkbox-before-label row as other form switches
     (verso-field); this block, not the gate, carries the change hooks.

     The gate and whichever branch is showing are fields like any other: the
     gate brings its own cell of air, a note about the state the toggle is in
     belongs to the toggle and runs on as its next line, and a field-set the
     toggle reveals is more rows of the form, each with its own cell of air.
     So the block adds no air of its own. */}}
<div class="verso-conditional" data-verso-change-field data-verso-change-name="{{.Name}}" data-verso-change-label="{{.Label}}" data-verso-change-kind="toggle">
  {{.Gate}}
  {{/* A revealed field-set carries its own rows, and a field row zeroes its top
       padding when it is first — so the standing-off is this block's to state. */}}
  {{/* A gate with nothing to reveal is just its row: an empty reveal would
       still hang its standoff under the row when switched on. */}}
  {{if .Fields}}<div class="verso-conditional-body verso-rhythm">{{range .Fields}}{{.}}{{end}}</div>{{end}}
  {{if .Otherwise}}<div class="verso-conditional-otherwise verso-rhythm">{{range .Otherwise}}{{.}}{{end}}</div>{{end}}
</div>
